# Tests that fail on a loaded host although the code under test is right: they wait for
# a process, a lock or a deadline in wall time, so their outcome depends on how busy the
# machine is. One test function name a line, as it is written after `fn` in a file of this
# directory; `#` starts a comment, and blank lines are skipped.
#
# What the list is for: a run that must not read load as a verdict skips these names or runs
# them apart, one at a time. The mutation driver is to pass them as `--skip` filters and to
# rerun alone a mutant that only they caught; the gate is to run them under
# `--test-threads=1`. Nothing reads this list yet: neither the mutation driver nor the gate
# consumes it as of 0.11.1.
#
# How a name gets on it: a failure of the test under load, recorded with the run that showed
# it (a command and its log), while the test passes on the same tree on an idle host. A name
# that is here because the code is slow is a finding about the code, not an entry. The test
# `the_load_sensitive_list_names_tests_that_exist` (in agent_hook.rs) fails when a name here
# is no test function of this directory.
#
# Each name says under a comment how it got here. The first five: measured 2026-11-25 from the
# kept logs of the mutation campaign over 0.10.0's changes: each is a `test <name> ... FAILED`
# line in 19, 16, 16, 12 and 1 of them, all logs of mutants in the patch crate's parser and the
# projection crate's side-by-side view, and these five are the only failing tests those logs
# hold.
